JOUKJ wrote:
> At least for me it is less tiring for my eyes : It save me a headache
> not having to look at a too light screen, on which the less important
> thing (the background) is (hi-)lighted.


For VT terminals, this was definitely the case.

However, for GUI displays with greater sharpness, despite what one
"feels", the white background/withe text is the best for an office
environment. Your pupils are smaller due to greater amount of light and
thus you see sharper text. And when you switch from screen to
desk/paper, there is less of a dramatic change.

If you work in a dark environment (think air traffic controllers in an
underground windowless envrionment), then things are guite different and
the dark background becomes better.

Another problem with web pages is that there are pages where they
purposefully put the background black, but use javascript to set text
colour to white, but if you have javascript disabled, the text is black
on a black background :-)


