Well I've solved the problem by some miracle!

I've removed the Accton cards and replaced the D-Link DFE500TX rev. C-2
card in the machine. I restarted the system, and this card has been
recognised correctly by the SRM console as a DECchip 21140-AA card!

I've no idea what happened, although since I last tried this card I have
removed an Adaptec 2940U/UW SCSI controller that was unrecognised by
SRM. As such I've been able to turn pci_parity back on, and I'll give
the accton cards one last try and report back. Maybe it'll help someone
else in the future.

Cheers,
Steve
