  I don't know of a generic high-level introduction to OpenVMS internals
  that's at all current here -- without intending offense, the concept
  of a "high-level internals introduction" is one I have trouble wrapping
  my head around.  Most  everything I have on the local booksheves are 
  likely rather more detailed than you seem to want here.  (I'd tend to
  start with the IDSM, too -- once you involve the concept of "internals",
  the complexity of the discussion tends to increase rather rapidly, and
  the IDSM is the central "internals" discussion and documentation.)

  Here are some potential resources:

  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Openvms

  VAX/VMS Software Handbook (1981, ancient, maybe enough here?)

  What most folks use is the IDSM, of course -- more details
  than you want, but it's the central resource for the kernel.

  It would not surprise me that there's an OS-related textbook
  or two around with discussions of OpenVMS, as well.

