Now that you mention it, the only ones I've seen have a USB connector to plug
into the computer and either 25- or 50-pin SCSI on the other end for a device.
Oh, well, that's what I get for thinking out of the box.  Definitely out of the
box.

How about a SCSI device that accepts various and sundry flash cards including
PCMCIA, CF, SD, and probably some others?  Yes, those do exist.  The simplest
one for the world of VAXen would be one which accepts only one type of card,
like a PCMCIA flash card.  Otherwise, the devices which support multiple card
types usually enumerate themselves with multiple LUNs.  And there are also
adapters for PCMCIA flash card slots to handle CF (like from my digital camera)
and other flash form factors.

Argus and Microtech are two brand names for these devices, which can be found on
eBay.  The devices are probably out of manufacture, which is too bad.  They work
very nicely.  There are both internal and external ones... Ben Myers

