Bob Koehler wrote:
>    I'm trying to get a hardware maintenance contract from HP.  One of
>    my systems, an Infoserver-1000, has the following model number on
>    its tag:
> 
>       70-30343-03. A02
> 
>    HP claims that "703034303A" is not a valid model number.
> 
>    Is this a punctuation problem, or is HP looking for some other
>    number?
> 

Look at the bottom of your Infoserver 1000.  Hopefully it should have a 
sticker with TWO entries for the model number and the 70-30343-03 A02 is 
the bottom one and in parenthesis.  As others have stated, the number 
you need will be of the format SEADx-xx.  The 70-30343-03 is really the 
"option" part number of the daughter card that plugs onto the Infoserver 
motherboard that provides your console, ethernet and power connections 
(in the case of the 70-30343-03, this is the AUI variant).  There are 
also variants of those daughter cards options that are Thinwire and one 
that plugs into the Infotower.

70-30343-01  SEADB, standalone thinwire
70-30343-03  SEADC, standalone AUI
70-30343-04  Infotower



