To the list:

I recently got an EV67 XP1000.  I was getting it together and was
surprised to find no AlphaBios.  Apparently it was never offered for
this model.  There is an NT compatible SRM for the EV6 model (which I
also have)  I wondered if that SRM was compatible with the ev67 - in
other words, is this a marketing issue or a technical one?

I swapped CPU boards.  Neither box would boot to console with the wrong
CPU board - the leds would light up, stack from bottom to top, but the
boot process never got as far as loading the graphic card bios and
starting up the monitor.

This is pretty interesting.  It looks to me like the EV67 firmware may
be incompatible with that for EV6.  Furthermore, I'm thinking that if I
tried to force it by installing on the EV67 machine the NT-compatible
version of the 5.9 SRM firmware from a bootable floppy, it would either
not load, or it would load and leave me with a computer that could not
access its own drives so as to revert to its former firmware ...  or
maybe I could get it to boot but only with the EV6 CPU board.

Any thoughs on this issue?  I'd like to be able to run some windows
programs on this box, as well as Linux and Tru64.  It does not look
very likely, though.

PS while I was Googling for information, I found a bunch of Terry
Shannon's old newsletters .. damn, I miss him!

jn



